    thinking: "**Defining Frontend Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the frontend\'s architecture. My focus now is defining the necessary features. I\'m starting with a multi-tier role switcher and subsidiary filter. I\'m breaking down the role selection component, which is the cornerstone of this module, and how it will interact with the other components.\n\n\n**Mapping User Roles**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the user roles: Colliery Manager, Safety Officer, and Overman, considering their relationship to Corporate HQ and Regulatory Authorities. I\'m now developing the Mine Block Selector. I\'m thinking about the real-time indicators such as the live status, AI risk levels, and even emergency alerts.\n\n\n**Visualizing Mine Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the GIS spatial mine map and its interactive layers. The goal is to provide a visual representation of both the surface and subsurface layout. I\'m incorporating layer toggles for risk heatmaps, gas zones, and inspection findings, along with drone survey overlays. I\'m also thinking about clickable inspection pins that instantly display evidence and status.\n\n\n\n**Developing Compliance Frameworks**\n\nI\'m now integrating compliance features. I\'m focusing on pre-configured checklists for safety and environmental aspects across various mining operations: Opencast, Underground, and Environmental Monitoring. I\'m also addressing offline functionality with a local IndexedDB sync queue. I am designing a Statutory Compliance and Digital Registers module for paperless governance, including key forms and reports.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Compliance Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-powered OCR for statutory notices. It\'ll automatically handle DGMS violation letters, extracting crucial data and generating action items with assigned engineers. Additionally, I\'m incorporating an AI Mining Governance Copilot for instant queries on regulations and auto-drafting action reports. I\'m also developing a Contractor & Labor Compliance Portal that covers safety scorecards, digital rosters, and more, including a gate-pass blocking mechanism. I am designing an automated workflow system, escalation matrix, and CAPA matrix with digital signatures. Lastly, a technical guide and architecture blueprint for enterprise backend integration is in development.\n\n\n**Building Backend Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the production backend. I\'m finalizing API schemas, database models, and deployment runbooks for downloadable documentation. I am also working on creating clean, modular files. I\'m focusing on defining the data structures, realistic mock data for Indian coal mining, and UI components such as header and command hub. I am developing an interactive GIS spatial mine map component, as well as a field inspection interface.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 743521138
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
